From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/25] Build a real Krama generator engine and regenerate RV
 1.1 from it

Responds to the project lead's detailed review, which correctly identified
generate_krama_rv_1_1.py as a hand-aligned transcription (hardcoded pairs/
PARIGRAHA_FORMS per verse) rather than a generator. Adds three modules:

- sanskrit_phonology.py: a real sandhi engine (samhita_join, resolve_compound)
  covering Patala 2's vowel classes and Patala 4's visarga/consonant rules,
  validated 69/70 against DGE's own attested samhita_patha for RV 1.1.
- pratishakhya_classify.py: predicate functions (is_pragrhya, is_rephi,
  requires_parigraha, get_sthita/get_upasthita/get_sthitopasthita) replacing
  flat Pragrhya/Rephi word lists, each stating what it still cannot derive.
- krama_engine.py: generate_ardharca/generate_verse, computing base pairing
  (10.2) and Parigraha (10.7-10.9, 10.12-10.14, 10.16) from real predicates,
  plus a computational reconstruction of sutra 10.3's aa-monosyllable
  exception from Uvata's own worked example. split_into_ardharcas() finds
  ardharca boundaries automatically using DGE's attested samhita_patha only
  as a length-alignment oracle (never to look up pair content), correct on
  7/9 of RV 1.1's verses unaided.

Found and fixed a real bug while writing tests/test_krama_engine.py's
regression case: the 10.3 special-case branch skipped the 10.9
ardharca-final Parigraha check entirely.

regenerate_krama_rv_1_1.py runs this pipeline directly against DGE's
Pada-patha/Samhita-patha (no per-verse word list typed anywhere in it) and
compares against the old hand-aligned output: 7 of 9 verses match exactly;
the other 2 surface one real improvement (10.3 correctly generalizing to a
second case in 1.1.2) and one genuine open phonological gap (visarga before
aa in 1.1.7 not matching DGE's attested "bharanta emasi", documented rather
than patched blindly).

validate_krama_rv1_1.py implements the spec's own Test A-H suite in its
required INPUT/EXPECTED/GENERATED/STATUS/APPLIED RULES/TRANSFORMATIONS/WHY
format: A-E pass against the real engine; F/G/H (Samhita-vs-Pada restoration,
bahumadhyagata auto-detection, Suddhakshara restoration) are honestly
reported UNRESOLVED, since no function for any of them exists yet.

Architecture doc (sec.6.6) and PENDING.md updated with full detail on what's
covered, what's an open gap, and what's still Priority-0/1 future work.

